<code>assert \forall int i; index<=i && i<\old(this.size()); (this.get(i) == (\old(this.get(i-1))==null ? null : \old(this.get(i-1))));</code>

This assertion seems to be incorrect based on the description in the comment. Let's correct it to accurately reflect the intended specification.

The comment states that for every valid index from the specified index to the old size of the list, the element at the next position is either null if the old element at this position was null, or it equals the old element at this position. However, this doesn't quite match the operation of inserting an element, which shifts elements to the right.

A more accurate assertion would be that for every valid index from the specified index to the old size of the list, the element at the current position is equal to the old element at the previous position.

Here is the corrected assert statement:

<code>assert \forall int i; index<i && i<=\old(this.size()); this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i-1));</code>

This asserts that for every index `i` greater than the specified `index` and less than or equal to the old size of the list, the element at position `i` is equal to the element at position `i-1` before the insertion.
